      "post_subject": "question about boric acid",
      "content_md": "Kodak F5 Hardening Fixer doesn't seem to be available anymore, but I do have the formula from a book. It calls for boric acid, but the author says to use the crystalline form, and avoid the powdered type. It seems that the chemical suppliers offer two types, either \"boric acid\" or \"boric acid, granular.\" I haven't bought this chemical before, so I'm guessing that the \"ordinary\" type is crystalline, and the granular form is powdered. Does anyone know? Thanks in advance.",
